WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.141 --> 00:00:05.635
- Sinnah, sometimes I get tired

00:00:05.635 --> 00:00:08.659
of pursuing my passion of rapping.

00:00:08.659 --> 00:00:10.955
I'm wondering right now,
should I take a break,

00:00:10.955 --> 00:00:13.249
or keep at it; if so, how long?

00:00:13.249 --> 00:00:15.575
I get afraid of falling behind.

00:00:15.575 --> 00:00:17.408
Much love to you guys.

00:00:18.856 --> 00:00:20.081
- [Stephen] Yeah, that's
a good question, Sinnah,

00:00:20.081 --> 00:00:23.647
I think, um, you know, if
you love what you're doing,

00:00:23.647 --> 00:00:26.828
whatever it is, rapping, let's take that.

00:00:26.828 --> 00:00:30.923
You probably need to say,
are you really energized?

00:00:30.923 --> 00:00:34.346
Are you fresh, are you um, really focused

00:00:34.346 --> 00:00:36.093
on achieving your goals?

00:00:36.093 --> 00:00:39.599
And invariably, there comes
a time where you kind of

00:00:39.599 --> 00:00:42.249
run out of a bit of energy,
and you need to have a bit of,

00:00:42.249 --> 00:00:44.991
kind of recharge and reflection.

00:00:44.991 --> 00:00:49.089
So um, at those points, you
know, whatever works for you,

00:00:49.089 --> 00:00:51.608
you can go on vacation, whatever, um,

00:00:51.608 --> 00:00:54.400
get together with friends, you
go and see mentors, you know,

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.981
whatever it is that really works for you,

00:00:56.981 --> 00:00:59.905
and then uh, and then I
think that's a great time

00:00:59.905 --> 00:01:02.887
to reflect on kind of what's working,

00:01:02.887 --> 00:01:04.499
fundamentally to still believe

00:01:04.499 --> 00:01:07.018
in your big idea, um, and if you do,

00:01:07.018 --> 00:01:10.072
what do you need to change to
make it even more successful?

00:01:10.072 --> 00:01:13.907
And then you kind of can
get right back into it.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.190
- This is an interesting one, cause we're,

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:18.016
we're just about to release
a video on Lindsey Stirling,

00:01:18.016 --> 00:01:19.023
I don't know if you know Lindsey,

00:01:19.023 --> 00:01:21.531
but she's, she's a violinist,

00:01:21.531 --> 00:01:25.921
and she had one of the
top YouTube videos, uh,

00:01:25.921 --> 00:01:29.623
for one of her songs, and
when she was doing violin,

00:01:29.623 --> 00:01:32.343
she kind of got bored
of it, because it was

00:01:32.343 --> 00:01:35.074
kind of classical and the same thing,

00:01:35.074 --> 00:01:37.444
and she just really grew tired of it,

00:01:37.444 --> 00:01:40.007
and she wanted to put it
down, and then she discovered

00:01:40.007 --> 00:01:42.599
electronic music and Skrillex and DJs,

00:01:42.599 --> 00:01:46.600
and all of these people putting
out beats, and she said,

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.637
"That'd be really cool
to combine my violin

00:01:49.637 --> 00:01:51.319
"with the electronic beats."

00:01:51.319 --> 00:01:53.938
And she formed a new thing
that hadn't existed before,

00:01:53.938 --> 00:01:56.759
and that reignited her
interest and passion in violin,

00:01:56.759 --> 00:01:58.792
and also helped her differentiate herself

00:01:58.792 --> 00:02:02.468
and create one of the top
YouTube videos for music videos.

00:02:02.468 --> 00:02:03.719
And so I'm wondering if there,

00:02:03.719 --> 00:02:06.124
there might be something
like that in it for you,

00:02:06.124 --> 00:02:07.505
where if you still love rapping,

00:02:07.505 --> 00:02:08.959
but you're not, you know, you don't like

00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:10.299
doing it the way you've been doing it,

00:02:10.299 --> 00:02:12.220
or the way other people are doing it,

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:15.260
to explore, maybe combine it
with another passion of yours,

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:18.079
to continue to test the waters.

00:02:18.079 --> 00:02:20.383
You know, if you look at The Beatles,

00:02:20.383 --> 00:02:22.947
none of their albums
sounded like each other,

00:02:22.947 --> 00:02:25.417
the first album was way
different than the next one,

00:02:25.417 --> 00:02:26.715
and way different than the next one,

00:02:26.715 --> 00:02:28.045
and people are like "Well, why don't,

00:02:28.045 --> 00:02:30.352
"we like the early Beatles, why
don't you keep doing those?"

00:02:30.352 --> 00:02:33.287
Well we've grown as people,
we don't do that anymore,

00:02:33.287 --> 00:02:34.932
we want to do new stuff, and I think

00:02:34.932 --> 00:02:37.987
that's part of every
entrepreneur, especially artists,

00:02:37.987 --> 00:02:41.319
you have to continue to evolve
and test and try new things,

00:02:41.319 --> 00:02:42.794
and so, if you're getting a little bored

00:02:42.794 --> 00:02:44.783
of what you're doing, I'd say,

00:02:44.783 --> 00:02:47.450
"How do I mix in something new?"

00:02:48.593 --> 00:02:50.814
Try out a new project that
still involves the rapping,

00:02:50.814 --> 00:02:52.792
but you can involve,
incorporate something else in it

00:02:52.792 --> 00:02:55.778
to push yourself and see
if it makes you come alive.

00:02:55.778 --> 00:02:57.628
- [Stephen] Yeah, I
think that's good, Evan,

00:02:57.628 --> 00:03:01.063
I think also, if you're
really getting bored,

00:03:01.063 --> 00:03:04.251
go and kind of, go, go round and listen

00:03:04.251 --> 00:03:08.479
to rappers you really respect,
go and meet some of them.

00:03:08.479 --> 00:03:11.079
Um, maybe, maybe think
about doing something

00:03:11.079 --> 00:03:13.662
collaboratively with a partner,

00:03:14.513 --> 00:03:16.207
cause it sounds like you
just need new innovation,

00:03:16.207 --> 00:03:18.186
it sounds like you've got a core idea,

00:03:18.186 --> 00:03:20.433
you love what you're doing,
but if you need to evolve,

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:23.016
there's loads of opportunities.

